                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "87015814-5fa1-3181-aefd-72d74019f00c",
                        "entry_id": "4c4d2309-55f3-3d77-b6cb-269bdf254f55",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To speak, write or behave in a Hemingwayesque manner."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cec38c4e-e072-4363-a623-1e3a6af06248",
                                "sense_id": "87015814-5fa1-3181-aefd-72d74019f00c",
                                "text": "But there is no literary law that says thai — to set forth these beauties — the writers must first excel in the art of Hemingwaying."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f280006-5898-4792-a9d1-71868f3f9246",
                                "sense_id": "87015814-5fa1-3181-aefd-72d74019f00c",
                                "text": "Ivens concluded his account with a remark that out-Hemingwayed Hemingway: 'I know that money is hard to make but dying is not easy either."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0efc1bb1-0408-4e1a-819c-87f0d22a9cf5",
                                "sense_id": "87015814-5fa1-3181-aefd-72d74019f00c",
                                "text": "That just-a-moment had hardly died away before Father turned and Hemingwayed Bogoljub so forcefully that the tobacconist was sent flying against the bookshelves."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "434881d7-8567-443a-bf96-6efee804df8c",
                                "sense_id": "87015814-5fa1-3181-aefd-72d74019f00c",
                                "text": "And as it turned out, he'd Hemingwayed his so-called past. Those tales he told about backpacking the two-thousand-mile-long Appalachian Trail while fighting off bears and wolves? The time at Pismo Beach when he punched out a shark to rescue a lifeguard? The stories were interesting the first few times I heard them but they paled with the retelling."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d8ae9c07-b0fd-3ced-99b6-36b9dda3c194",
                        "entry_id": "4c4d2309-55f3-3d77-b6cb-269bdf254f55",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To study, or talk about, Ernest Hemingway."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "892c6f4b-fc0d-4d1d-9cf9-b0df05de7c6e",
                                "sense_id": "d8ae9c07-b0fd-3ced-99b6-36b9dda3c194",
                                "text": "After Hemingway's death in 1961, he was bombarded with questions about the author and finally asked a reporter to let it be known that he was “Hemingwayed out!”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0679328-ca54-4220-8d44-5f9cbad17b7e",
                                "sense_id": "d8ae9c07-b0fd-3ced-99b6-36b9dda3c194",
                                "text": "Lena knew more about the missing stories than 98 percent of the people who Hemingwayed for a living."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b9d0274-bd10-4c85-9692-a23ee2305993",
                                "sense_id": "d8ae9c07-b0fd-3ced-99b6-36b9dda3c194",
                                "text": "I said, “I'm a little Hemingwayed out, but we can go to Floridita after dinner if you'd like.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
